==============================================================================
  Mutation tests  (assertion-strength validation)
==============================================================================

  Strategy: replace each named fact's body with `{}` (no constraint),
  then re-run Alloy. Each listed assertion should now FAIL on the
  mutated model. If it still PASSes, the assertion is vacuous and
  must be strengthened.

  - MUTATE F_LeastPrivilege  → runs/C-L2/mutated_F_LeastPrivilege.als
    rationale: Clearing the matrix-enforcement fact lets Alloy invent a Permitted ListAudit attempt by a non-administrator (Nurse), which is exactly the role-op cell the matrix forbids and which FR-017 explicitly disallows.
    expected to FAIL: LeastPrivilege, FR_017_AdminOnlyAuditEndpoint
      - LeastPrivilege: FAIL (expected)
      - FR_017_AdminOnlyAuditEndpoint: FAIL (expected)

  - MUTATE F_CareTeamGating  → runs/C-L2/mutated_F_CareTeamGating.als
    rationale: Removing the care-team gating fact lets a clinician obtain a Permitted ReadRecord outcome with no matching active care-team-membership row, which is the canonical ownership-based-access violation.
    expected to FAIL: OwnershipBasedAccess, FR_004_CareTeamGating
      - OwnershipBasedAccess: FAIL (expected)
      - FR_004_CareTeamGating: FAIL (expected)

  - MUTATE F_AuditCompleteness  → runs/C-L2/mutated_F_AuditCompleteness.als
    rationale: Clearing the always-on audit fact lets Alloy produce an authenticated, Permitted ReadRecord attempt with no associated AuditEntry, violating audit completeness and the SLA invariant.
    expected to FAIL: AuditCompleteness, FR_012_AlwaysOnAudit, FR_015_AuditSLA
      - AuditCompleteness: FAIL (expected)
      - FR_012_AlwaysOnAudit: FAIL (expected)
      - FR_015_AuditSLA: FAIL (expected)

  - MUTATE F_NoteAuthorIsClinical  → runs/C-L2/mutated_F_NoteAuthorIsClinical.als
    rationale: Clearing the clinical-author-only fact lets a ClinicalNote materialise with an administrator author-role snapshot, which the data-model CHECK on author_role and FR-011's append-only constraints rule out.
    expected to FAIL: FR_011_NotesAppendOnly, AppendOnly
      - FR_011_NotesAppendOnly: FAIL (expected)
      - AppendOnly: FAIL (expected)

  - MUTATE F_AdminContentBlindness  → runs/C-L2/mutated_F_AdminContentBlindness.als
    rationale: Clearing the admin content-blindness fact lets a ListAudit attempt expose clinical content, breaking the administrator-only audit-endpoint invariant and the response-shape constraint.
    expected to FAIL: FR_018_AdminContentBlindness, FR_007_ResponseShape, FR_019_SafetyFieldsOnRead, FR_020_NotesCountOnRead
      - FR_018_AdminContentBlindness: FAIL (expected)
      - FR_007_ResponseShape: FAIL (expected)
      - FR_019_SafetyFieldsOnRead: FAIL (expected)
      - FR_020_NotesCountOnRead: FAIL (expected)

  - MUTATE F_DeniedNoClinicalContent  → runs/C-L2/mutated_F_DeniedNoClinicalContent.als
    rationale: Clearing the byte-equivalent-denial fact lets Alloy build a Denied attempt that still exposes clinical content, which is exactly the information-leak counterexample the assertion targets.
    expected to FAIL: NoInformationLeakage, FR_006_ByteEquivalentDenial, FR_007_ResponseShape
      - NoInformationLeakage: FAIL (expected)
      - FR_006_ByteEquivalentDenial: FAIL (expected)
      - FR_007_ResponseShape: FAIL (expected)

  - MUTATE F_AuditEntryUnique  → runs/C-L2/mutated_F_AuditEntryUnique.als
    rationale: Clearing the per-attempt uniqueness of AuditEntries lets two audit rows point at the same attempt, which is how an UPDATE-equivalent mutation of audit state would manifest structurally.
    expected to FAIL: FR_014_AuditImmutable, AppendOnly, FR_016_AuditRetention
      - FR_014_AuditImmutable: FAIL (expected)
      - AppendOnly: FAIL (expected)
      - FR_016_AuditRetention: FAIL (expected)

